  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing the Participation of Women and CSOs in the Energy Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The projects purpose is to strengthen the engagement of CSOs in national development priorities in the areas of gender (Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) 5), energy (SDG7), environmental conservation (SDG15) and inclusive society for development (SDG16). The Action will support the Micronesia Conservation Trust (MCT)  as the lead applicant  to improve CSO linkages with the national and state governments of FSM through the delivery of this project, which will empower women and their communities, in the remote islands of Chuuk State, through the College of Micronesia  FSMs training program and solar electrification of their communities. The project is also sustainable over the long-term, and combines creating real, practical agency for women and their communities with stable access to clean energy that is both environmentally friendly and sustainable over time. The project will also improve livelihoods and income generating opportunities including empowerment of women on sustainable energy and energy efficiency.</narrative>
  </description>
